terests of consumers and promoting fair practices in the food trade across Europe. The establishment of EFSA was driven by increasing public concern regarding food safety crises, notably the BSE epidemic in the late 1990s, which underscored the need for a robust and independent scientific authority capable of providing credible risk assessments. 

